Print the stdout and stderr of a command started with anona-compute exec -b,
which keeps them in the sandbox under /tmp/anona-compute-bg. stdout goes to
stdout and stderr to stderr; a line on stderr says whether the process is
still running or how it exited.

  anona-compute exec -b ID -- 'npm run dev'      prints the PID
  anona-compute output ID PID                    everything so far
  anona-compute output ID PID -f                 follow until the process ends

With --json: one object {"pid","state","exit_code"?,"stdout","stderr"}; with
-f, {"type":"stdout"|"stderr","data"} lines and a final {"type":"exit",...}.
Processes started any other way have no saved output (anona-compute ps lists them).

Usage:
  anona-compute output SANDBOX_ID PID [flags]

Flags:
  -f, --follow        keep printing output until the process ends
  -h, --help          help for output
  -u, --user string   user to read the output as (default: the sandbox's default user)

Global Flags:
      --api-key string             API key (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_KEY, E2B_API_KEY)
      --api-url string             API URL (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_URL, E2B_API_URL; default https://api.<E2B_DOMAIN>)
      --json                       JSON output on stdout (same as -o json)
  -o, --output string              output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string             config profile to use (env ANONA_COMPUTE_PROFILE; default "default")
      --request-timeout duration   timeout for each API request (0 = none)
  -v, --verbose                    verbose output on stderr
